{"game": "aliens-fireteam-elite", "language": "english", "appid": 1549970, "month": "2023-03", "window": 2, "start_date": 1678233600, "end_date": 1678924799, "month_true_total": 118, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-04 02:21:44 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "134698065", "author": {"steamid": "76561198981340230", "personaname": "Obozo Gaming", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Obozo_Gaming/", "num_games_owned": 463, "num_reviews": 47, "playtime_forever": 498, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 498, "last_played": 1678849180, "avatar": "c8b7a6de718bb1bfc4a6367ad073637a4c6fece1"}, "language": "english", "review": "I beat Fireteam a little less than twelve hours ago and have this to say. I love the Alien movies. This game wants to be fun. And it is, but only with friends. But it's really repetitive. \"Hey. Go here, press a button, kill enemies, go to a new location, press a button, kill enemies.\" it's like that for every mission. And there are games that have made it fun, but each mission I flipped my brain off. The locations are interesting, but at the same time boring. It's either spaceship, ruins, or Alien Hive.  While the game is a step up from Alien: Colonial Marines, and it can be fun. But I do not recommend it unless the game's on sale and you have friends to play it. I hope if they make a second Fireteam, they improve upon what's here.", "timestamp_created": 1678883605, "timestamp_updated": 1678883605, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 3, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.515524804592132568", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1629777600", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 6, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "134657679", "author": {"steamid": "76561197996219005", "personaname": "Battlebrother Shorty", "persona_